From c7d11ab1a9eccad8885ca1a821be0706a7597900 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:56:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] UPCYLOFF: HOME start sends Off once to C_Load_Up / C_Empty_Up
 / C_Auto1_Up / C_Auto2_Up / C_Auto3_Up on HT9050 -- EastSun 1007
 (AskUserQuestion: at HOME start).

On HT9050 these are double-solenoid valves (C_xxx_Up + C_xxx_UpOff, IO_Table stations 176 / 177); Cylinder[] drives only the On coil, the Off coil has no engine object. uhome.cpp HOME step 1 calls g_W906UpCylOffHook(0): On coil off (Cylinder.Off() when the engine row is enabled, plus the IO write -- C_Empty_Up is engine-disabled with AUTO_EMPTY_COLOR=0) and Off coil on; every HOME pass calls g_W906UpCylOffHook(1), which releases the Off coil after 500 ms so a later On never finds both coils energised. The hook body is at the end of JsonBridge/IoBtnPanelClick.cpp (same IO write as io.btnPanelClick), registered by a static initializer; 0 in ctests. HT9050 (9050GPIB or Type_HT9050) only. Same lines + end of file. HOME-related tests passed (none drives the hook; check on the machine). Debug and release linked. WORKLOG row 193.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
